{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility","id":1470325,"title":"Of Strangers and Shoggoths (On Chimeras and Fae Whimsy vs Utility)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-12T20:00:23-08:00","id":1470325,"title":"Of Strangers and Shoggoths (On Chimeras and Fae Whimsy vs Utility)","content":"Was advised to move this discussion from the Simple Question thread to avoid clutter; conversation can be picked up later, but my weekend is almost over, so I figured I should get this typed up while it was fresh in my mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470193#post1470193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While I like our current version of Chimera, I wonder why it was changed from this version?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because getting arguably the best dice trick in the game on every form of rolled supernatural evasion for one of the most easily-procured supernatural fuel sources in the setting is a bit much for an exclusive power that's already adding a global bonus to Social rolls with everything from the gameline's primary otherworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess this is a disconnect then, because I was under the impression that being mutable was a definite and defining quality in and of itself. Are you saying that\u2019s not the case? </div> </div> </div>If the only guaranteed thing about it is that nothing is guaranteed about it, it's not much of a quality.<br /> <br /> Look at myth and legend. Tam Lin is shapeshifted between a dozen different forms in his captors' bid to make his savior let him go. Sun Wukong can transform into anything that exists, animate or inanimate. Proteus, the god from which we get the word &quot;protean,&quot; turns into other things to keep from having to answer people's questions. Notice that most of these things are the result of directed divine or divine-adjacent power akin to Royal Contracts that turn you into specific things.<br /> <br /> On the other end of things, look at Demon, where the God-Machine's outlook is much closer to the bluntly practical concerns of &quot;this one worker needs to be able to handle multiple different problems.&quot; There's a demonic form ability that lets you change your other form abilities on the fly, but it's the highest-rated type of form ability, it can't be used outside of a full transformation, it takes Aether and an action for each swap, and you still have defaults that you need to reset to rather than swapping a form ability from one thing to another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean this is fair, but I guess I don\u2019t understand the Others mind set at all. I chose that background because of Shoggoths being a vaguely similar creature to what I was doing, and they were created and enslaved to basically serve a role. That role being whatever the Elder Things wanted at the time. (They are basically robots as I understand) I figured that worked well enough to port over to Changeling. (I don\u2019t read Lovecraft, really but I browse wikis sometimes) </div> </div> </div>Gonna dip into Mage for a momentary comparison and highlight the difference between The Abyss and (Greater) Abyssal Beings, because those operate at about the same cosmological level and you can replace &quot;The Abyss&quot; with &quot;Arcadia&quot; and still hit the same points of that I'm talking about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> The Abyss is the magic-adjacent part of reality where anything can happen; the laws of the universe change unpredictably, and it is very difficult to survive for any length of subjective time without a more powerful patron to support you. Fire might not warm you but instead cause you to turn transparent. Writing the word &quot;delicate&quot; might turn your bones to jelly. Reality is out to lunch.<br /> <br /> Abyssal Beings are the main powerful patrons that can offer stability in the greater Abyss, world-beings with consistent-enough personalities and metaphysics that you can get the hang of how they operate after enough time to acclimate much like you would anywhere on Earth. The Prince of a Hundred Thousand Leaves is alien to our reality, but it is reliably a cannibal timeline with its own bits of awful history that it tries to paste over ours when given the chance.<br /> <br /> The True Fae are not Arcadia. They are <i>parts of</i> Arcadia, and they express their desires within the limits they bargained their power from. They have Titles and Regalia and oaths that mean pursuing their Aspirations has to work around the limits they agreed to, which includes not having everything be anything all of the time. Their reality-warping is handled using the systems for Hedgespinning and oneiromancy, which can't trivially make substantial changes to important characters, and while that's obviously not the system they use to create changelings, it's still applied through the lens of the Fae's identity as a being with a Title based on an emotion, sensory experience, or object.<br /> <br /> The Name behind the Marchioness of Death In The Freezing Mountains may have a passing fancy for the warmth of a sunset across a desert plain, but she will need to use existing agreements to actualize that desire, and her Title may come with obligations that work directly against it. She may have to make overtures to the Princess of Burning Footsteps Pursued By Scorpions or make war on the Duke of the Scarlet Horizon for his lands and deeds, or satisfy her craving with bottled memories from other domains, but she's not going to turn her whole chunk of Faerie into the temperate and topological opposite of itself on a narrative timescale that can't be observed by anyone who's not plugged into the dream-machine that fools her servants into thinking she's omnipotent.<br /> <br /> A shoggoth is basically a giant genetically-engineered super-amoeba that accidentally attained sentience. The Elder Things made them through genetic engineering and mind control, because the Elder Things are not gods operating practically outside the constrains of material reality through conceptual bargains struck with mythic symbolism. If the True Fae were to have shoggoth-equivalents, they would more than likely be a type of hobgoblin, because turning humans into shapeless blobs of flesh is a little more Deviant (or Vampire or Demon) than Changeling, as sensibilities go.<br /> <br /> On a more general note, &quot;can survive in any environment and have some fun body horror with benefits&quot; is, now that I remember, reasonably close to describing certain aspects of the Elemental seeming \u2014 Primal Glory can cover a fair amount of ground for survivability, and the seeming's blessing is flavored such that the right choice of element can be proper spooky.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Employing Hobgoblins would make much more sense, but I get the impression asking one of the Kindly Ones to swallow their pride just won\u2019t happen unless they are forced to. </div> </div> </div>They're less prestigious to use for the same purposes as changelings, but if your goal is just to have somebody to handle the job then it doesn't really matter if they don't come from the other side of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the subject of contacts, this Kith really isn\u2019t that different from Talon and Wing. Talon and Wing doesn\u2019t explicitly say you can\u2019t get a creatures ability to survive in certain environments. </div> </div> </div>Talon and Wing doesn't explicitly say that because it instead explicitly says that the Contract can grant three different effects and describes what those effects are, with the sole example effect outside of that list being a seeming bonus, and there's a Common Contract for ignoring damage from particular bits of nature in another Regalia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (The only way I can kinda approach the Others mindset is assuming my desires are the only thing that matters, and nothing else is really\u2026real.) </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That's how they operate, generally. The Strangers' closest mundane analog is the hyper-rich, who include among their number the sort of person who buys rugs you would expect to find in a museum as regular replacements for something they could absolutely just use regular carpeting for (flooring a room in their yacht, if I'm remembering this specific example correctly).<br /> <br /> Later 2e supplements may shift exactly how accurate the technicalities of this description are, but there's a line in Mortal Remains that summarizes the True Fae as their own unfiltered self-images. They're bastards. They don't care. They set up a hundred-dozen agreements with the universe to specifically allow them to continue not to care. Some of those agreements <i>rely on</i> their never caring. That explanation I gave earlier about hobgoblin deals being designed to squeeze the non-goblin parties for everything they're worth? The Gentry play with that concept's meaner, nastier older sibling. You will serve until they're done with you.<br /> <br /> (And to expose my own &quot;might just be a 'me' thing&quot; here: I hate having to make changes to a thing that require me to first undo the work of the initial setup. It feels like going backwards and if you fuck it up you've added even more steps to the process. And this is for something less complicated than re-rigging a human being you took for one purpose to serve a completely different purpose that doesn't overlap at all. It's less trouble by far to start over from as close to the changeover point as you can get pre-made, especially given that you'll have to do that anyway if you bungle the undoing process.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The merit to modify dropping the mask is interesting. I don\u2019t think we have a merit for modifies the Mien when dropping the mask for benefits. It actually really suits a number of character archetypes like a berserker Beast or Ogre who want to drop the mask for a physical power boost even if they don\u2019t really use contracts. Do you think I should drop the kith in exchange for the merit? The kith could just be something like a Broadback or Cleverquick that really invests in that merit. </div> </div> </div>It would certainly get around the problem of figuring out what Skill the blessing benefited, if nothing else, and I'd been thinking of making a similar Merit for different purposes anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019d like to say I do like the pool of merits. I edited one of my previous posts, but I don\u2019t think you saw that. To reiterate, I had few extra merits I thought could be added, and asked about Beast\u2019s advanced merits. I looked to see if any conversation had emerged about using the Advanced Merits, and I saw a previous conversation on this very thread about them. Now I\u2019d like to ask if there is any reason not to port the Advanced Merits that don\u2019t use Beast specific mechanics over if I thought it could fit? </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470111#post1470111\">Looking at the edit,</a> I should point out that Hardy is already half-covered by the benefits of Wyrd, Freediving modifies a system that didn't exist in 2e until Deviant updated it, and Double-Jointed functionally removes the cost of Portaling out of a grapple in a way that doesn't feel like the kind of thing that comes as a side benefit.<br /> <br /> Double-Jointed (Advanced) is quite close to the 1e Tunnelgrub blessing, Direction Sense (Advanced) cuts into one of the printed example benefits of a personal oath and also a Royal Contract, and I feel like Iron Skin's general deal doesn't play nice with Changeling's standard methods of damage-avoidance at above-basic levels. Striking Looks (Advanced) feels conceptually iffy for changelings and rote quality is, as I mentioned up top, arguably the best dice trick in the game. Fast Reflexes (Advanced) should work fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T05:21:02-08:00","id":1470338,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t really have the time to get into a detailed response, but I think you very thoroughly answered all my possible concerns and questions. Thank you for writing this.<br /> <br /> I think I will actually be able to do stuff in two to three days, and I will see if we can get a working version of that merit going.<br /> <br /> Edit: I do think it will be cool to have our conversation about this all in one place, because you have written a lot of good analysis about Changeling over the course of our conversation and I\u2019d like people to see all of it. Maybe we can copy and paste or use links to mark the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-13-2021, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T11:25:48-08:00","id":1470536,"title":"","content":"I'm back. I have deeds to do, and promises to keep (I'm not dappled or drowsy or ready to sleep).<br /> Anyways<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was advised to move this discussion from the Simple Question thread to avoid clutter; conversation can be picked up later, but my weekend is almost over, so I figured I should get this typed up while it was fresh in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div> And I'm glad you did, since if we had been waiting on me, this conversation would have had to wait until now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably because getting arguably the best dice trick in the game on every form of rolled supernatural evasion for one of the most easily-procured supernatural fuel sources in the setting is a bit much for an exclusive power that's already adding a global bonus to Social rolls with everything from the gameline's primary otherworld.</div> </div> </div> </div> I suppose it is rather strong once you take into account Glamour's fuel efficiency, and harvestability. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the only guaranteed thing about it is that nothing is guaranteed about it, it's not much of a quality.</div> </div> </div> </div> I take your point. I don't think I completely agree, but you do have more experience with this in the context of Changeling. Also this seems to one of those arguments that goes in circles, and I'd like to avoid that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at myth and legend. Tam Lin is shapeshifted between a dozen different forms in his captors' bid to make his savior let him go. Sun Wukong can transform into anything that exists, animate or inanimate. Proteus, the god from which we get the word &quot;protean,&quot; turns into other things to keep from having to answer people's questions. Notice that most of these things are the result of directed divine or divine-adjacent power akin to Royal Contracts that turn you into specific things.</div> </div> </div> </div> ...that's fair. I had wondered if the concept was too strong for a kith. Granted some Kith trickeries are actually stronger than a Royal Contract. Looking at your examples, none of the various had shapeshifting as their nature, it was always either a skill or something completely external from them, much like the contracts as you mentioned. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other end of things, look at Demon, where the God-Machine's outlook is much closer to the bluntly practical concerns of &quot;this one worker needs to be able to handle multiple different problems.&quot; There's a demonic form ability that lets you change your other form abilities on the fly, but it's the highest-rated type of form ability, it can't be used outside of a full transformation, it takes Aether and an action for each swap, and you still have defaults that you need to reset to rather than swapping a form ability from one thing to another.</div> </div> </div> </div> Figures that my closest mindset to the True Fae would be closer to the God-Machine than the True Fae. I'm trying to not be amused by that. That being said, given the severe thematic differences between the God-Machine and the Others, (and Changeling and Demon in general) it does make sense that this isn't a thing the Strangers make. As for how the ability works in Demon, that seems to be because of Demon's modular nature. I think a ability closer to Changeling would be much more limited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gonna dip into Mage for a momentary comparison and highlight the difference between The Abyss and (Greater) Abyssal Beings, because those operate at about the same cosmological level and you can replace &quot;The Abyss&quot; with &quot;Arcadia&quot; and still hit the same points of that I'm talking about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> The Abyss is the magic-adjacent part of reality where anything can happen; the laws of the universe change unpredictably, and it is very difficult to survive for any length of subjective time without a more powerful patron to support you. Fire might not warm you but instead cause you to turn transparent. Writing the word &quot;delicate&quot; might turn your bones to jelly. Reality is out to lunch.<br /> <br /> Abyssal Beings are the main powerful patrons that can offer stability in the greater Abyss, world-beings with consistent-enough personalities and metaphysics that you can get the hang of how they operate after enough time to acclimate much like you would anywhere on Earth. The Prince of a Hundred Thousand Leaves is alien to our reality, but it is reliably a cannibal timeline with its own bits of awful history that it tries to paste over ours when given the chance.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah. That's disturbing that the similarities are great enough to make this comparison. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The True Fae are not Arcadia. They are <i>parts of</i> Arcadia, and they express their desires within the limits they bargained their power from. They have Titles and Regalia and oaths that mean pursuing their Aspirations has to work around the limits they agreed to, which includes not having everything be anything all of the time. Their reality-warping is handled using the systems for Hedgespinning and oneiromancy, which can't trivially make substantial changes to important characters, and while that's obviously not the system they use to create changelings, it's still applied through the lens of the Fae's identity as a being with a Title based on an emotion, sensory experience, or object.</div> </div> </div> </div> This the part I seem to have missed, that they must define themselves by Name and Title. I seem to have assumed that the Strangers could be little pockets of chaos that can be devoted entirely to their whims.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Name behind the Marchioness of Death In The Freezing Mountains may have a passing fancy for the warmth of a sunset across a desert plain, but she will need to use existing agreements to actualize that desire, and her Title may come with obligations that work directly against it. She may have to make overtures to the Princess of Burning Footsteps Pursued By Scorpions or make war on the Duke of the Scarlet Horizon for his lands and deeds, or satisfy her craving with bottled memories from other domains, but she's not going to turn her whole chunk of Faerie into the temperate and topological opposite of itself on a narrative timescale that can't be observed by anyone who's not plugged into the dream-machine that fools her servants into thinking she's omnipotent.</div> </div> </div> </div> So the Strangers are would have to acquire many Titles in order to have a seemingly constantly changing theme and narrative. And it would never be truly chaotic, as they would be limited to the narratives of their Titles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A shoggoth is basically a giant genetically-engineered super-amoeba that accidentally attained sentience. The Elder Things made them through genetic engineering and mind control, because the Elder Things are not gods operating practically outside the constrains of material reality through conceptual bargains struck with mythic symbolism. If the True Fae were to have shoggoth-equivalents, they would more than likely be a type of hobgoblin, because turning humans into shapeless blobs of flesh is a little more Deviant (or Vampire or Demon) than Changeling, as sensibilities go.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I did wonder if this concept was too close to Deviant. Guess that it's true then. I like the filtering of certain science fiction tropes through Changeling lens, and see what results. Guess that this one just didn't fit. Oh well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more general note, &quot;can survive in any environment and have some fun body horror with benefits&quot; is, now that I remember, reasonably close to describing certain aspects of the Elemental seeming \u2014 Primal Glory can cover a fair amount of ground for survivability, and the seeming's blessing is flavored such that the right choice of element can be proper spooky.</div> </div> </div> </div> That probably explains why Elementals have been persistently my favorite seeming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're less prestigious to use for the same purposes as changelings, but if your goal is just to have somebody to handle the job then it doesn't really matter if they don't come from the other side of the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talon and Wing doesn't explicitly say that because it instead explicitly says that the Contract can grant three different effects and describes what those effects are, with the sole example effect outside of that list being a seeming bonus, and there's a Common Contract for ignoring damage from particular bits of nature in another Regalia.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I'm just bemoaning that environmental adaptation isn't one of the effects listed. I just wish Primal Glory didn't have the thorns effect, I just want to breathe underwater, and not die of heat stroke, not kill anyone who tried to lay a finger on me. Plenty of animals have that, and Talon and Wing allows you grab certain animal parts for their benefits. It just makes conceptual sense to me that Talon and Wing would let you do that. Maybe another seeming bonus would let you. Ogre maybe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. That's how they operate, generally. The Strangers' closest mundane analog is the hyper-rich, who include among their number the sort of person who buys rugs you would expect to find in a museum as regular replacements for something they could absolutely just use regular carpeting for (flooring a room in their yacht, if I'm remembering this specific example correctly).</div> </div> </div> </div> While I'm not surprised by your example as something that has happened, I have a feeling that actually getting details on it will just anger me. I dislike waste of resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Later 2e supplements may shift exactly how accurate the technicalities of this description are, but there's a line in Mortal Remains that summarizes the True Fae as their own unfiltered self-images. They're bastards. They don't care. They set up a hundred-dozen agreements with the universe to specifically allow them to continue not to care. Some of those agreements <i>rely on</i> their never caring. That explanation I gave earlier about hobgoblin deals being designed to squeeze the non-goblin parties for everything they're worth? The Gentry play with that concept's meaner, nastier older sibling. You will serve until they're done with you.</div> </div> </div> </div> This explains a lot, and is terrifying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And to expose my own &quot;might just be a 'me' thing&quot; here: I hate having to make changes to a thing that require me to first undo the work of the initial setup. It feels like going backwards and if you fuck it up you've added even more steps to the process. And this is for something less complicated than re-rigging a human being you took for one purpose to serve a completely different purpose that doesn't overlap at all. It's less trouble by far to start over from as close to the changeover point as you can get pre-made, especially given that you'll have to do that anyway if you bungle the undoing process.)</div> </div> </div> </div> I hope I haven't caused too much annoyance on this front, since I think you had to explain several concepts repeatedly for me to understand both them and your point through them. That being said, I can understand why restarting after making progress would be tiresome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would certainly get around the problem of figuring out what Skill the blessing benefited, if nothing else, and I'd been thinking of making a similar Merit for different purposes anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then lets do that. On a side note, do I have your permission to post the Polychromatic version you created on the new Kiths topic? I would like to see what others think of it and it is somewhat buried in our conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1470111#post1470111\">Looking at the edit,</a> I should point out that Hardy is already half-covered by the benefits of Wyrd, Freediving modifies a system that didn't exist in 2e until Deviant updated it, and Double-Jointed functionally removes the cost of Portaling out of a grapple in a way that doesn't feel like the kind of thing that comes as a side benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure Hardy stacks with Wyrd, making it at least worth looking at if you don't want fatigue penalties. Freediving is the closest I could think of not outright giving someone gills, and being a mundane merit. As for Double-jointed...yeah. I think Double Jointed absolutely is in theme, but the conflict with Portaling is not something I'm completely comfortable with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility#post1470325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Double-Jointed (Advanced) is quite close to the 1e Tunnelgrub blessing, Direction Sense (Advanced) cuts into one of the printed example benefits of a personal oath and also a Royal Contract, and I feel like Iron Skin's general deal doesn't play nice with Changeling's standard methods of damage-avoidance at above-basic levels. Striking Looks (Advanced) feels conceptually iffy for changelings and rote quality is, as I mentioned up top, arguably the best dice trick in the game. Fast Reflexes (Advanced) should work fine.</div> </div> </div> </div> So the Advanced merits are conceptually on par with 1e Kiths. A 2e version of Tunnelgrub would be very interesting, since part of their niche is now available to everyone through Portaling. Maybe there should be a different &quot;Advanced&quot; merit that builds off of Portaling and Double Jointed to be the ultimate escape artist merit. There should be some Merit or Contract that drops the Mask in order to show off the Mien for social purposes. Wasn't there a series of Contracts in 1e to do this? Direction Sense (Advanced) doesn't make thematic sense for the Lost, I would agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T12:38:50-08:00","id":1470548,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem is similar to what Aquatosic faced with the multi-limbered kith: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468754#post1468754\">you're focusing on form, not function</a>. It is better since you decided to narrow it to survival adaptation, but you're still trying to squeeze too much from the form instead of saying what this shapechanging does effectively for the story.<br /> <br /> Tam Lin is changed to make holding him as undesirable or cumbersome as possible, it is the crux of the <i>challenge</i> his savior must overcome. Sun Wukong uses it to hide his identity, it is his signature ability as a <i>liar</i>. Shoggoths are the greatest creation of the Elder Things, and destroyed their creators with it, it makes them <i>apex monsters</i>. Some legendary creatures that live in dreams change to grant desire or cause fear, it is a tool of <i>emotion</i>. Gods and their servants in many myths change to interact with mortals, it serves <i>communication</i>.<br /> <br /> Observe that no one does everything with such power. The more complex, nuanced or simply powerful a creature, the more tangential a power to change shape actually is. They all change for real, but the new forms aren't deemed all-purpose tools, instead they are very specialized for each one, in and out of character.<br /> <br /> Use this. Instead of trying to figure out how to make a character that can assume any shape, start to think what your kith gets out from its ability to assume any shape. Make <b>this</b> specific and let go other functions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T16:59:41-08:00","id":1470561,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve rewritten many responses to this well written post, in the end it all boils down to: do you believe that being a <b>survivor</b> is too broad a concept to define a character? Should I be trying to narrow the focus down further or trying to unite the Trickery and blessing to being able to survive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T19:18:05-08:00","id":1470577,"title":"","content":"Here is a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1469725#post1469725\">link</a> to a few posts before the start of this discussion with TempleBuilder back in the Simple Questions thread, from which one can also reach my explanation of Goblin Debt and the link to a post where I quoted some Hunter fiction dealing with an extended interaction with a Goblin Market.<br /> <br /> Here is a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468654#post1468654\">link</a> to me talking about designing a multi-armed kith, from which one can also reach Arc's post explaining several important differences between Changeling and Demon.<br /> <br /> Here is a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1468726#post1468726\">link</a> to me talking about incubi, quoting the introduction of the term in 1e, and discussing its likely viable translations to 2e's systems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility?p=1470536#post1470536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Figures that my closest mindset to the True Fae would be closer to the God-Machine than the True Fae. I'm trying to not be amused by that. That being said, given the severe thematic differences between the God-Machine and the Others, (and Changeling and Demon in general) it does make sense that this isn't a thing the Strangers make. As for how the ability works in Demon, that seems to be because of Demon's modular nature. I think a ability closer to Changeling would be much more limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that really helps to contextualize the God-Machine is that the vast majority of its holdings are completely nonmagical, and a lot of the magical bits are only magical when they're producing an effect \u2014 take apart an occult matrix and you have a bunch of ordinary materials, with maybe one or two bits of Weird Stuff that nevertheless fails to cause a supernatural outcome on its own.<br /> <br /> Unless it would be more efficient to use a supernatural actor for a given configuration of Infrastructure (e.g. sending an angel to do the job of a mortal allows three intersecting plans to be advanced at the same time), the God-Machine will use ordinary people and materials that can do the job cheaply and on-schedule to the degree that produces the desired output and no further. (It's not hard to see why some demons Fall from trying to do their jobs better, given this tendency.)<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the True Fae are egomaniacal desire-made-flesh dealing with emotion-based fuel in a magic-rich environment backed by a framework of obligations to legendry and palpable phenomena. They want things. They have people for that. The Wyrd gave them a ruleset so complex no one of them could comprehend it all just as the God-Machine stewards a system of arcane physics so complex no one person could fully grasp it. Pursuing personal advancement comes naturally to them and if they aren't fixated on a particular facet of their surroundings it can be replaced as needed, including captive changelings they've lost interest in. Magic is easy to pick as a first resort if violence or intrigue or raw charm aren't your speed. Preternatural talent in particular fields is easier to find; that's one of the things that kiths represent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah. That's disturbing that the similarities are great enough to make this comparison. </div> </div> </div>There is some overlap in Changeling 1e's descriptions of the sort of weird world-going-slightly-<i>off</i> omens that presage the True Fae's arrival and Mage's <i>Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss</i>'s general advice for creating and introducing Abyssal beings into a story, and while Dancers in the Dusk introduced a Morphean who's pretty clearly the dream-level reflection of the Aeon of the Abyss I'm still fond of analogizing Changeling's magical framework as the Abyss-adjacent god-magic to Mummy's Lower Depths-adjacent god-magic, particularly after Mysterious Frontiers's treatment on mages in the Hedge confirmed that 2e still has the Hedge resonate pretty strongly with the Abyss, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1062344-grimoire-of-cursory-dissection-a-thread-for-personal-musings?p=1404863#post1404863\">to say nothing of the services the locals offer to visitors</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This the part I seem to have missed, that they must define themselves by Name and Title. I seem to have assumed that the Strangers could be little pockets of chaos that can be devoted entirely to their whims. </div> </div> </div>Nope; the 2e corebook goes over this, and in general terms (if not entirely specific mechanics) it largely agrees with 1e's material in Equinox Road. There's a bit in that book that does note they could theoretically do anything outside of those constraints, but they wouldn't have any <i>consequences</i> \u2014 it would be indistinguishable from a person entertaining a particularly vivid fantasy in the privacy of their own mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the Strangers are would have to acquire many Titles in order to have a seemingly constantly changing theme and narrative. And it would never be truly chaotic, as they would be limited to the narratives of their Titles. </div> </div> </div>Alternately, they would have to leverage a great many pacts and pledges to secure secondhand access to a breadth of motifs beyond those of their own Titles. The True Fae aren't exactly consistently social creatures, but they <i>do</i> inhabit a framework of agreements that often involves others of their kind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I'm just bemoaning that environmental adaptation isn't one of the effects listed. I just wish Primal Glory didn't have the thorns effect, I just want to breathe underwater, and not die of heat stroke, not kill anyone who tried to lay a finger on me. Plenty of animals have that, and Talon and Wing allows you grab certain animal parts for their benefits. It just makes conceptual sense to me that Talon and Wing would let you do that. Maybe another seeming bonus would let you. Ogre maybe? </div> </div> </div>I would imagine Elementals or Ogres, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This explains a lot, and is terrifying. </div> </div> </div>Like, I want to underline this, for all that it might be invalidated later in the current edition: 1e Changeling introduced Charlatans, True Fae who (to simplify immensely) basically <i>started to care about people</i> and consequently lost most of their power and memories of Arcadia in exchange for an easier time surviving the mortal world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope I haven't caused too much annoyance on this front, since I think you had to explain several concepts repeatedly for me to understand both them and your point through them. That being said, I can understand why restarting after making progress would be tiresome. </div> </div> </div>Not at all, I can handle repetition just fine; it's the effective multiplication of task-length that gets to me \u2014 Do Route A, Undo Route A, Do Route B, and the linking of the two Routes makes it feel like stretching the same task out instead of three separate actions (or five, seven, nx+1, etc). Intellectually I get that there's no actual difference, but the direct link from one step to another and the knowledge that some of those steps are purely damage-control for bad decision-making/poor planning does something in my brain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then lets do that. On a side note, do I have your permission to post the Polychromatic version you created on the new Kiths topic? I would like to see what others think of it and it is somewhat buried in our conversation. </div> </div> </div>By all means, with the caveat that it <i>is</i> a first draft; being able to shed emotional Conditions entirely may be a bit strong, given how that affects Hedge travel and the consequences of Hedgespinning paradigm shifts, so I'd maybe switch the Trickery's effect to suppressing an emotional Condition a la the Cold Hearted Merit for Clarity Conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There should be some Merit or Contract that drops the Mask in order to show off the Mien for social purposes. Wasn't there a series of Contracts in 1e to do this? </div> </div> </div>About half of the clauses for the Contracts of Vainglory, whose closest 2e equivalents are Mantle of Terrible Beauty to Paralyzing Presence (which applies the Cowed Condition on an exceptional success, including those gained by using the Contract while the Mask has been scoured away) and Splendour of the Envoy's Protection to The Royal Court (which changed to be unrolled and affect a gathering, which in turn means using it when you've dropped your Mask makes you more effective at Social Maneuvering against one witness).<br /> <br /> The main thing is that, since the worst consistent consequences of dropping the Mask is applying the Spooked Condition, that <i>is</i> showing off the Mien for social purposes; given the requirements for striking a bargain and the additional Clarity-healing criteria wild entitlements provide, I think it's reasonable to say that witnessing an unMasked changeling is not consistently a breaking point against Integrity, given ChroD Core's guidelines of &quot;witness[ing] something traumatic, terrifying, or that rattles [your] understanding of the world&quot; or &quot;[being] the victim of a supernatural attack, whether physical, emotional, or mental.&quot;<br /> <br /> (The encounter might <i>go on</i> to induce breaking points from those things, and seeing the actual act of burning away the Mask might itself be distressing, but just seeing a person with pointy ears and bug-eyes walking around less so.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Forgot to finish a paragraph. 12-16-2021, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T04:41:27-08:00","id":1470611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470325-of-strangers-and-shoggoths-on-chimeras-and-fae-whimsy-vs-utility?p=1470561#post1470561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve rewritten many responses to this well written post, in the end it all boils down to: do you believe that being a <b>survivor</b> is too broad a concept to define a character? Should I be trying to narrow the focus down further or trying to unite the Trickery and blessing to being able to survive?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you must focus. Not necessarily narrow it down, but focus. Stop thinking of it as &quot;the kith of shapechanging blobs&quot; and start to think of it as &quot;the kith of extreme adaptation&quot;, that so happens to do this by being shapechanging blobs. Stop treating the shapechanging as the main aspect at all.<br /> <br /> That way you'll have not only a narrower scope to make effects, but a tangible, interesting theme to create descriptions, think of origins, make it unique instead of generic. It is not just that the bonus is to survival, is that the <b>theme</b> is survival. And instead of changing shape because their Keepers are <i>that</i> lazy, they change shape because their environment was <i>that hardcore</i><i> and unstable</i>. Or they had to explore extreme places. Whatever it is, it becomes and active direction instead of a directionless benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}